            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5"
          ],
          "text": "CT abdomen confirmed adhesional small bowel obstruction with a transition point identified and no ischaemia on initial imaging. He was initially managed conservatively with nasogastric tube and drip and suck. Warfarin was held and his INR reversed in anticipation of surgery. He subsequently underwent emergency laparotomy with adhesiolysis, resection of a non-viable segment of small bowel, primary anastomosis, and formation of a defunctioning loop ileostomy. He recovered post-operatively in HDU. Stoma nurse teaching was commenced prior to discharge. Metformin, ramipril, and bisoprolol were restarted on day 6; warfarin was restarted with bridging treatment-dose enoxaparin until his INR becomes therapeutic.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
